body:
Hm, it seems that the `NoSuchMethodException` occurs during `InMemoryStorageService` injection, but only if that bean contains a method annotated with `@Gauge`. If I remove the gauge, it works. But right now I have no idea why that happens, especially since it's in native mode only.
At build time, we dynamically attach an interceptor binding (`MetricsBinding`) to beans that contain a Gauge, but that's basically all that happens specifically to such beans at build (we don't actually register/initialize the gauge until the bean is instantiated). Perhaps it has something to do with that.

Anyway if it is necessary to fix quickly, I have a workaround for now: remove the `@Gauge` annotation from the `size()` method and instead register the gauge by including this in `InMemoryStorageService`:

```
@Inject
MetricRegistry metricRegistry;

@PostConstruct
public void sizeGauge() {
	metricRegistry.register(this.getClass().getName() + ".size", (org.eclipse.microprofile.metrics.Gauge<Long>) this::size);
}
```

It should be pretty much equivalent.

OK, actually this isn't a bug in Quarkus. 

It's just that the pattern used in the application needs a small fix in order to work in native mode.

Due to the use of:

```
	@Produces
	@ConfiguredStorage
	public StorageService createStorage(@Any Instance<StorageService> instance) {
		if (StorageServiceProducer.PERSISTENT.equals(storageType)) {
			return instance.select(PersistentStorageService.class).get();
		}
		return instance.select(InMemoryStorageService.class).get();
	}
```

it's expected that `InMemoryStorageService` and `PersistentStorageService` can be created from the default constructor.

To make that possilble in native mode, these classes need to be annotated with `@RegisterForReflection(fields = false, methods = true)`.

So I am going to close the issue as it's not a bug, however I would like @manovotn or @mkouba to comment on `StorageServiceProducer` which is:

```
public class StorageServiceProducer {

	private static final String INMEM = "inmem";
	private static final String PERSISTENT = "persistent";

	private final String storageType;

	@Inject
	public StorageServiceProducer(
			@ConfigProperty(name = "sample.storage.type", defaultValue = StorageServiceProducer.INMEM) String storageType) {
		this.storageType = storageType;
	}

	@Produces
	@ConfiguredStorage
	public StorageService createStorage(@Any Instance<StorageService> instance) {
		if (StorageServiceProducer.PERSISTENT.equals(storageType)) {
			return instance.select(PersistentStorageService.class).get();
		}
		return instance.select(InMemoryStorageService.class).get();
	}

}
```

I think that there is a way to better do it at build time, but it's late Friday and my brain is fried :P
If we don't have support for the build time determination of such a pattern, I really think we should add it since it seems to be a common need.
